---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "October 12, 2026";
---

<Layout title={`Privacy Policy | ${site.name}`} description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" dim="Policy.">
    <p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="light" data-nav="light">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how {site.name} (“we”, “us”, “our”) collects, uses and protects personal information when you visit our website, contact us, book a call, or work with us on GoHighLevel and workflow automation projects.</p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Information you send us:</b> when you use our contact form we collect your full name, business email, company or agency name, the service you need, your estimated timeline and any project details you share. We also keep the emails and messages you send us.</li>
        <li><b>Booking information:</b> when you book a call through our scheduling tool (Cal.com), the details you enter, such as your name, email, chosen time and notes, are processed by that provider and shared with us.</li>
        <li><b>Technical information:</b> our hosting provider automatically records standard server logs, such as IP address, browser type, pages visited and the time of the visit. Our fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address when the page loads.</li>
        <li><b>Client project data:</b> when we work inside your systems (for example your CRM, automations or email platform), we may access personal data you control, such as your leads and customers. See section 6.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your enquiries and schedule calls.</li>
        <li>To scope, deliver, document and support the services you hire us for.</li>
        <li>To send invoices, updates and project communication.</li>
        <li>To keep our website and systems secure and working properly.</li>
        <li>To meet legal, tax and accounting obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
      <p>Our website does not use advertising or analytics cookies. Third-party tools embedded on the site, such as our booking popup, may set their own cookies to work. Their use is governed by their own privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We only share information with service providers that help us run our business, and only as much as they need:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Website hosting (Hostinger)</li>
        <li>Scheduling (Cal.com)</li>
        <li>Email and communication providers</li>
        <li>CRM and automation platforms we use to manage enquiries and projects (for example GoHighLevel)</li>
        <li>Font delivery (Google Fonts)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, or as part of a merger, sale or transfer of our business.</p>

      <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
      <p>We work with clients worldwide, and our service providers may process data in countries other than your own. We take reasonable steps to make sure your information stays protected wherever it is processed.</p>

      <h2>6. Data we handle for clients</h2>
      <p>When we build or maintain systems for you, we access your data only as needed to do the agreed work, follow your instructions, keep it confidential, and do not use it for any other purpose. You remain responsible for having a lawful basis to collect and process the personal data stored in your own systems.</p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes above. Enquiries that don’t lead to a project are usually deleted within 24 months. Project and billing records are kept as long as required for legal and accounting purposes.</p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information, including access controls and secure, reputable service providers. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your personal information, to object to or restrict how we use it, and to withdraw consent. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>10. Children</h2>
      <p>Our services are for businesses and are not directed at children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date above shows when it was last changed.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy? Email us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
